### REST Client API Tests (Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
# Replace this token with an actual ID token obtained from your Firebase frontend
@firebaseIdToken = your_firebase_id_token_here

### 1. Login (Sync Firebase User with MongoDB)
# This will verify the Firebase ID token and return your user profile from the database.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}

###

### 2. Get Current User Profile (Me)
# Retrieves your user profile from MongoDB using the same Firebase ID token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}

###

### 3. Logout
# Logs the user out. (Note: Since we use Firebase tokens, logout revokes refresh tokens on the server, but your client frontend must also sign out of Firebase).
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}
